node_modules/
dist/
*.db
*.db-wal
*.db-shm
# `.env` alone did not cover `.env.local`, which is where a real key ended
# up. The negation keeps the one env file that is meant to be committed
# committable -- `.env*` would otherwise silently ignore a template someone
# adds later, which is the failure this pair exists to avoid in both
# directions.
.env*
!.env.example
/config/
/secrets/
# The host derives its artwork directory from the database path, so the
# `npm run dev` database at the repo root puts artwork here rather than beside
# a container's `/config/pickarr.db`. Created on the first artwork fetch, not
# at boot, so it appears partway through a dev session.
/artwork/

# Playwright run output (traces, screenshots, HTML report)
test-results/
playwright-report/

# SDD process scratch (ledgers, briefs, review packages)
.superpowers/
